/*!
    \page sonicipc-index.html
    \title Sonic IPC

    Sonic IPC is a small inter-process communication library for SonicDE. It
    is built on Unix domain sockets (QLocalServer / QLocalSocket). Components
    can talk to each other directly, peer to peer, without a message bus, so
    D-Bus becomes an option rather than a requirement.

    \list
    \li \l Sonic::Ipc::Server listens on a local socket and wraps each client
        in a \l Sonic::Ipc::Connection.
    \li \l Sonic::Ipc::Client connects to a server, optionally reconnecting
        across restarts, or sends one blocking request.
    \li \l Sonic::Ipc::Connection sends and receives frames, and tells the uid,
        gid and pid of the process at the other end.
    \endlist

    Each frame carries the application's protocol version and a message type.
    Damaged, oversized or foreign data is rejected and the connection closed; a
    peer speaking another protocol version is told so first. Frame type
    0xFFFFFFFF is reserved for the library.

    \code
    constexpr quint16 protocolVersion = 1;

    auto *server = new Sonic::Ipc::Server(this);
    server->listen(Sonic::Ipc::Server::userSocketPath(QStringLiteral("my-service.sock")),
                   Sonic::Ipc::Server::Access::User, protocolVersion);
    connect(server, &Sonic::Ipc::Server::newConnection, this, [](Sonic::Ipc::Connection *connection) {
        QObject::connect(connection, &Sonic::Ipc::Connection::frameReceived, connection,
                         [connection](quint32 type, const QByteArray &payload) {
                             connection->send(type, payload); // echo
                         });
    });
    \endcode

    \section1 Using the Module

    \section2 Building with CMake

    Use the \c find_package() command to locate the SonicIpc package and link
    against its target:

    \badcode
    find_package(SonicIpc REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(mytarget PRIVATE Sonic::Ipc)
    \endcode

    \section1 API Reference

    \list
        \li \l{Sonic IPC C++ Classes}
    \endlist
*/
